{
 "nodes": [
  {
   "nodeID": "226",
   "text": "Is China on track to meet its Phase One purchase commitments?",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "question",
   "toulmin": "framing",
   "oper": "framing",
   "localID": "setser_jul_8_20#Q"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "227",
   "text": "Agriculture and energy flow through a few state firms, so purchases can be directed; manufacturing cannot",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "stated_assumption",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_jul_8_20#P1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "228",
   "text": "A deal with numerical targets may be judged on those targets alone",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "hidden_assumption",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_jul_8_20#P2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "229",
   "text": "The deal's own numbers — a 2017 baseline, roughly $60bn above it, a $164.65bn target across the codes in Annex 6.1",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "benchmark",
   "toulmin": "backing",
   "oper": "backing",
   "localID": "setser_jul_8_20#BM"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "230",
   "text": "Services excluded because in-China sales are not exports; aircraft adjusted out; only the listed HS codes counted",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "scope_choice",
   "toulmin": "qualifier",
   "oper": "qualifier",
   "localID": "setser_jul_8_20#SCP"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "231",
   "text": "First-half pace implies ~$83bn, below the 2017 baseline of ~$101bn and even below 2019; energy at 7% of its target; 1m barrels a day at $40 still yields only $7.36bn",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_jul_8_20#E1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "232",
   "text": "PIIE purchase tracker; Reuters on crude loadings; S&P Global on cancelled LNG cargoes; IMF growth forecast",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_source",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_jul_8_20#E2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "233",
   "text": "There is no policy lever in manufacturing — import substitution continues and trade does not run through a few buyers",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_jul_8_20#M1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "234",
   "text": "Seasonality blocks catch-up, and because targets are nominal a commodity price crash widens the gap without any change in volume",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_jul_8_20#M2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "235",
   "text": "Category by category: manufacturing will not close the gap, agriculture is behind but Q4 is still live, energy is effectively impossible",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "intermediate_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.step",
   "localID": "setser_jul_8_20#C1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "236",
   "text": "The deal is failing on its own terms — insisting on impressive numbers made the shortfall easy to demonstrate",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "main_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.final",
   "localID": "setser_jul_8_20#K"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "237",
   "text": "Raised up front and rebutted: \"the purchase commitments themselves were a mistake\" and \"COVID-19 changed everything\". A barrier-removal deal might have worked — but would not have produced a big number",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "opposing_view",
   "toulmin": "rebuttal",
   "oper": "rebuttal",
   "localID": "setser_jul_8_20#X"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "238",
   "text": "Agriculture could still deliver in Q4, which creates a real cost to abandoning the deal now",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "caveat",
   "toulmin": "qualifier",
   "oper": "qualifier",
   "localID": "setser_jul_8_20#QF"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "239",
   "text": "The aircraft collapse is exogenous — the largest category fell with the 737 MAX grounding, not with the deal",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "other_explanation",
   "toulmin": "rebuttal",
   "oper": "rebuttal",
   "localID": "setser_jul_8_20#R1"
  },
